\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Love divine, that stooped  to share
\par Our sharpest pang, our bitterest tear,
\par On Thee we cast each earth-born care;
\par We smile at pain while Thou art near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Though long the weary way we tread,
\par And sorrow crown each lingering year,
\par No path we shun, no darkness dread,
\par Our hearts still whispering: Thou art near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When drooping pleasure turns to grief,
\par And trembling faith is changed to fear,
\par The murmuring wind, the quivering leaf,
\par Shall softly tell us: Thou art near
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. On Thee we fling our burdening woe,
\par O Love divine, for each dear;
\par Content to suffer, while we know,
\par Living and dying, Thou art near\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

